From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: wake the interface's txq on its own AC's pass

__ieee80211_wake_txqs() runs once per AC. For the interface's own txq
(multicast and broadcast) it cleared the dirty mark before checking that
the pass is for that txq's AC, so the voice pass, which runs first, used
up the mark of the best-effort txq without waking it, and the best-effort
pass then found nothing to wake.

Check the AC first.

From OddBlueDog/openwrt milkflint-25.12 395, re-anchored here.
Downstream patch, no upstream equivalent: absent from mainline
(v6.18, v7.0, v7.2-rc4, v7.3, v7.4-rc4) and from wireless-next HEAD on
2026-11-28. Taken from OddBlueDog/openwrt milkflint-25.12, commit de3a6294d690;
no stable or mainline tracking, so drop it by hand if a real fix lands.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -373,9 +373,13 @@
 		/* txq and txq_mgmt are mutually exclusive */
 		WARN_ON_ONCE(vif->txq_mgmt);
 
-		if (!test_and_clear_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags) ||
-		    (ps && atomic_read(&ps->num_sta_ps)) ||
-		    ac != vif->txq->ac)
+		/*
+		 * Check the AC first: this runs once per AC, and clearing the bit
+		 * on another AC's pass would lose the wake-up.
+		 */
+		if (ac != vif->txq->ac ||
+		    !test_and_clear_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags) ||
+		    (ps && atomic_read(&ps->num_sta_ps)))
 			txqi = NULL;
 	} else if (vif->txq_mgmt) {
 		txqi = to_txq_info(vif->txq_mgmt);
